   "id": 666553,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the output?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">def update_hour():\n&nbsp;&nbsp;tmp = hour\n&nbsp;&nbsp;if is_dst:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;tmp += 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;else:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;tmp -= 1\n\nis_dst = True\nhour = int(input(\"Enter hour: \"))\nupdate_hour()\nprint(\"New hour:\", hour)\n</pre>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328712,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">New hour: 9</code>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The global variable hour is not edited in <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">update_hour()</code>. <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">tmp</code> is the local variable edited. <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">tmp</code> is discarded after <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">update_hour()</code> finishes."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328713,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">New hour: 10</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The global variable hour is in the print statement but not edited in update_hour()."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328714,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Error</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "tmp is a local variable in update_hour(). hour is a global variable. Neither variable is accessed out of scope."
    }
